export default {"en":{"labels":{"RA":"Right atrium","LA":"Left atrium","RV":"Right ventricle","LV":"Left ventricle","IVS":"Interventricular septum","aorta":"Aorta","pulmonary_trunk":"Pulmonary trunk","SVC":"Superior vena cava","IVC":"Inferior vena cava","mitral":"Mitral valve","tricuspid":"Tricuspid valve","aortic":"Aortic valve","pulmonary":"Pulmonary valve","SA_node":"Sinoatrial node","AV_node":"Atrioventricular node","His_bundle":"Bundle of His","left_bundle_branch":"Left bundle branch","right_bundle_branch":"Right bundle branch","LAD":"Left anterior descending artery","left_circumflex":"Left circumflex artery","right_coronary":"Right coronary artery","accessory_pathway":"Accessory atrioventricular pathway","Bachmann_bundle":"Bachmann bundle","brachiocephalic_artery":"Brachiocephalic artery","left_common_carotid":"Left common carotid artery","left_subclavian":"Left subclavian artery","diagonal_branch_1":"First diagonal coronary branch","diagonal_branch_2":"Second diagonal coronary branch","right_marginal":"Right marginal coronary branch"},"notes":{"RA":"Systemic venous blood returns here through the venae cavae. Right atrial pressure drives filling across the tricuspid valve when it exceeds right ventricular pressure.","LA":"Oxygenated blood returns from the lungs through the pulmonary veins. Its a, c and v pressure waves reflect atrial contraction, valve bulging and filling against a closed mitral valve.","RV":"The right ventricle pumps venous blood into the low-pressure pulmonary circulation. Its thin wall generates much lower pressure than the left ventricle.","LV":"The left ventricle supplies the systemic circulation. Its thick myocardium shortens and thickens during systole; cavity volume falls only when blood leaves through an open or incompetent valve.","IVS":"The muscular septum separates the ventricles and carries the bundle branches on its endocardial surfaces. Normal ventricular activation reaches the septum before spreading through the free walls.","aorta":"The elastic aorta stores part of the stroke volume during ejection and maintains flow during diastole. Aortic valve closure produces the dicrotic notch in its pressure trace.","pulmonary_trunk":"The pulmonary trunk carries deoxygenated blood from the right ventricle to the lungs. The pulmonary valve opens when right ventricular pressure exceeds pulmonary arterial pressure.","mitral":"The two mitral leaflets separate the left atrium and ventricle. They close when ventricular pressure exceeds atrial pressure; chordae and papillary muscles restrain prolapse rather than pulling the valve open.","tricuspid":"The tricuspid valve permits right atrial blood to enter the right ventricle. Pressure reversal closes it; the subvalvular apparatus prevents prolapse into the atrium.","aortic":"The aortic valve opens only when left ventricular pressure exceeds aortic pressure. Its closure begins isovolumetric relaxation and contributes the A2 component of S2.","pulmonary":"The pulmonary valve opens when right ventricular pressure exceeds pulmonary arterial pressure. Closure contributes the P2 component of S2.","SA_node":"The sinoatrial node normally initiates each heartbeat. Spontaneous phase-4 depolarization brings nodal cells to threshold without a stable resting membrane potential.","AV_node":"Slow atrioventricular nodal conduction delays ventricular activation, allowing time for ventricular filling. The PR interval includes atrial and His–Purkinje conduction as well as the AV nodal delay.","His_bundle":"The His bundle connects the AV node to the bundle branches across the fibrous skeleton. Complete AV block can leave the ventricles dependent on a slower escape pacemaker.","conduction":"The specialized conduction network distributes activation rapidly toward the ventricular endocardium. Depolarization then spreads from endocardium to epicardium; epicardial action potentials are shorter, allowing the repolarization sequence to reverse.","valves":"Chordae tendineae attach atrioventricular leaflets to papillary muscles. They prevent systolic prolapse; opening and closure remain passive consequences of pressure gradients.","coronary":"Coronary vessels supply the myocardium itself. Left coronary perfusion is favored during diastole because systolic contraction compresses intramyocardial vessels.","vessels":"Great vessels connect the cardiac chambers to the systemic and pulmonary circulations. Flow follows the local pressure gradient through the available outflow pathway."},"phaseNotes":["Atrial contraction adds the final portion of ventricular filling.","Ventricular pressure rises while cavity volume remains constant when all valves are competent and closed.","Ventricular blood exits through the semilunar valves during rapid ejection.","Ejection continues at a declining rate as ventricular activation subsides.","Ventricular pressure falls while cavity volume remains constant when all valves are competent and closed.","Atrial pressure exceeds ventricular pressure and drives rapid passive filling.","Filling slows as atrial and ventricular pressures approach one another, and continues until the next atrial contraction."]},"zh":{"labels":{"RA":"右心房","LA":"左心房","RV":"右心室","LV":"左心室","IVS":"室间隔","aorta":"主动脉","pulmonary_trunk":"肺动脉干","SVC":"上腔静脉","IVC":"下腔静脉","mitral":"二尖瓣","tricuspid":"三尖瓣","aortic":"主动脉瓣","pulmonary":"肺动脉瓣","SA_node":"窦房结","AV_node":"房室结","His_bundle":"希氏束","left_bundle_branch":"左束支","right_bundle_branch":"右束支","LAD":"前降支","left_circumflex":"左回旋支","right_coronary":"右冠状动脉","accessory_pathway":"房室旁路","Bachmann_bundle":"巴赫曼束","brachiocephalic_artery":"头臂干","left_common_carotid":"左颈总动脉","left_subclavian":"左锁骨下动脉","diagonal_branch_1":"第一对角支","diagonal_branch_2":"第二对角支","right_marginal":"右缘支"},"notes":{"RA":"体循环静脉血经上下腔静脉回流至此。右心房压力高于右心室压力时，血液通过三尖瓣进入右心室。","LA":"含氧血经肺静脉回流至此。a、c、v 波分别反映心房收缩、瓣膜向心房膨出以及二尖瓣关闭时心房持续充盈。","RV":"右心室将静脉血泵入低压肺循环。其心室壁较薄，产生的压力显著低于左心室。","LV":"左心室向体循环供血。收缩期厚实的心肌缩短、增厚；只有血液经开放或关闭不全的瓣膜流出时，心腔容积才会下降。","IVS":"室间隔分隔左右心室，其心内膜面走行左右束支。正常心室激动先到达室间隔，随后传播至心室游离壁。","aorta":"弹性主动脉在射血期暂时储存部分搏出血量，并在舒张期维持血流。主动脉瓣关闭与主动脉压力曲线上的重搏切迹相对应。","pulmonary_trunk":"肺动脉干将右心室的去氧血送往肺。右心室压力超过肺动脉压力时，肺动脉瓣开放。","mitral":"二尖瓣分隔左心房与左心室。当心室压力超过心房压力时瓣膜关闭；腱索与乳头肌防止瓣膜脱垂，并不主动拉开瓣膜。","tricuspid":"三尖瓣允许右心房血液进入右心室。压力梯度反转时瓣膜关闭，瓣下结构防止瓣膜脱垂入心房。","aortic":"左心室压力高于主动脉压力时，主动脉瓣才开放。其关闭标志着等容舒张开始，并参与形成第二心音的主动脉瓣成分 A2。","pulmonary":"右心室压力高于肺动脉压力时，肺动脉瓣开放。其关闭参与形成第二心音的肺动脉瓣成分 P2。","SA_node":"窦房结正常情况下启动每次心搏。结细胞没有稳定的静息电位，4 期自动去极化使膜电位逐渐达到阈值。","AV_node":"房室结的慢传导延迟心室激动，为心室充盈提供时间。PR 间期还包括心房和希氏—浦肯野系统的传导时间，不能全部等同于房室结延搁。","His_bundle":"希氏束跨越纤维骨架，将房室结与左右束支连接。完全性房室传导阻滞时，心室可能依赖较慢的逸搏起搏点。","conduction":"特殊传导网络将激动快速传向心室心内膜。随后去极化由心内膜向心外膜传播；心外膜动作电位较短，使复极顺序能够反转。","valves":"腱索连接房室瓣与乳头肌，防止收缩期瓣膜脱垂。瓣膜开闭仍是压力梯度驱动的被动过程。","coronary":"冠状血管供应心肌自身。左冠状动脉灌注主要发生在舒张期，因为收缩期心肌内血管受到压迫。","vessels":"大血管将心腔与体循环、肺循环连接。血流沿局部压力梯度经可用的流出通路运动。"},"phaseNotes":["心房收缩完成心室末期充盈。","所有瓣膜正常关闭时，心室压力升高而心腔容积保持不变。","快速射血时，心室血液经半月瓣流出。","心室激动逐渐消退，射血继续但速率下降。","所有瓣膜正常关闭时，心室压力下降而心腔容积保持不变。","心房压力高于心室压力，推动快速被动充盈。","心房与心室压力逐渐接近，充盈减慢，并持续到下一次心房收缩。"]}};
